1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:05,320
In my family, when the phone rings after 10, somebody

2
00:00:05,320 --> 00:00:08,380
is sitting in a room with a table, two chairs, and a man

3
00:00:08,380 --> 00:00:10,690
telling them this is their only chance.

4
00:00:11,060 --> 00:00:14,150
I know that room. I sat in it at 17.

5
00:00:14,600 --> 00:00:17,500
Nobody asked me what happened, not the police, not the

6
00:00:17,500 --> 00:00:20,430
prosecutor, not even the lawyer I paid.

7
00:00:20,840 --> 00:00:22,810
Nobody asked what happened.

8
00:00:23,070 --> 00:00:29,220
Let me tell you where we're from first, because nobody

9
00:00:29,220 --> 00:00:31,190
in those rooms ever did.

10
00:00:31,940 --> 00:00:36,200
On our block, you learn the sound of gunshots before you

11
00:00:36,200 --> 00:00:37,350
learn your times tables.

12
00:00:38,240 --> 00:00:41,700
Cars slow down for no reason, somebody's cousin didn't

13
00:00:41,700 --> 00:00:46,130
make it home. Last summer, the police take 40 minutes,

14
00:00:46,200 --> 00:00:49,860
they stay calm. So people get protection however they

15
00:00:49,860 --> 00:00:55,060
can. Nobody's thinking about paperwork, they're thinking

16
00:00:55,060 --> 00:00:58,130
about getting home alive.

17
00:00:59,300 --> 00:01:02,460
When the danger is that close, being safe matters more

18
00:01:02,460 --> 00:01:06,820
than being legal. And a lot of people in danger aren't

19
00:01:06,820 --> 00:01:08,950
even old enough to be legal yet.

20
00:01:09,160 --> 00:01:12,010
That's not an excuse, it's the truth.

21
00:01:12,460 --> 00:01:14,330
Nobody puts in the report.

22
00:01:15,200 --> 00:01:18,410
The Bible has a word for people like us, the oppressed.

23
00:01:19,420 --> 00:01:22,340
Under-protected when we call for help, over watched when

24
00:01:22,340 --> 00:01:25,470
we're just standing outside, over punished when we slip,

25
00:01:25,720 --> 00:01:28,940
and with no opportunities to get out from under any of

26
00:01:28,940 --> 00:01:32,300
it. The police don't come when we need them, but they

27
00:01:32,300 --> 00:01:36,520
come for us. It started under a picture online, two girls

28
00:01:36,520 --> 00:01:38,810
I barely knew decided I was the problem.

29
00:01:39,060 --> 00:01:41,540
Comments turned into messages, messages turned into I

30
00:01:41,540 --> 00:01:42,730
know where you stay.

31
00:01:43,080 --> 00:01:45,760
Then came a house party, I didn't go looking for them,

32
00:01:45,760 --> 00:01:46,960
they came looking for me.

33
00:01:46,960 --> 00:01:49,890
Both of them were 19, I was 17.

34
00:01:49,900 --> 00:01:53,990
The first one swung, the bottle was already in my hand.

35
00:01:54,300 --> 00:01:57,740
When it was over her tooth was gone, and I was the one

36
00:01:57,740 --> 00:02:01,610
the police wanted. They didn't find me on their own.

37
00:02:01,780 --> 00:02:05,450
The girls gave them my relatives information.

38
00:02:06,200 --> 00:02:08,870
Jada, Jada went to school with them.

39
00:02:09,260 --> 00:02:12,340
Her mother got on the phone and made her give the police

40
00:02:12,340 --> 00:02:15,310
my name and where I lived.

41
00:02:16,620 --> 00:02:19,510
Jada and I haven't talked since.

42
00:02:20,820 --> 00:02:24,690
One phone call can change who your family is to you.

43
00:02:25,540 --> 00:02:28,750
The report said I hit her with a bottle, that was true.

44
00:02:29,240 --> 00:02:32,040
It didn't say she came at me first, it didn't say there

45
00:02:32,040 --> 00:02:35,830
were two of them. Felonious assault, one night in jail.

46
00:02:39,980 --> 00:02:43,060
I didn't wait for a public defender, I paid for a lawyer

47
00:02:43,060 --> 00:02:53,160
myself. Me, 17 years old, 1 ,600 at the front, and the

48
00:02:53,160 --> 00:02:56,030
remainder of 10 ,000.

49
00:02:56,100 --> 00:02:58,990
Every dollar I worked for it.

50
00:02:59,600 --> 00:03:03,930
I met him for maybe 10 minutes at a time, twice.

51
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:09,320
Always in passing. He had a stack of folders under his

52
00:03:09,320 --> 00:03:12,760
arms and a suit on with a white shirt and a red tie.

53
00:03:12,760 --> 00:03:15,350
Usually blue or gray pants.

54
00:03:16,660 --> 00:03:19,670
And my folder was just one of them.

55
00:03:19,840 --> 00:03:22,060
He never asked me what happened once.

56
00:03:22,060 --> 00:03:26,660
He never asked about the messages or that there were two

57
00:03:26,660 --> 00:03:29,150
of them or who swung first.

58
00:03:29,400 --> 00:03:33,800
And it's quite odd because he read the reports from the

59
00:03:33,800 --> 00:03:37,960
both of them and that didn't trigger in his mind looking

60
00:03:37,960 --> 00:03:42,850
at the date of birth and the reports that I have injunct.

61
00:03:43,960 --> 00:03:47,210
All he said is... There's a youth program.

62
00:03:47,560 --> 00:03:50,770
LAWYER: Plead, finish your probation, and it comes off your record.

63
00:03:51,040 --> 00:03:53,670
LAWYER: Fight it, and you're betting your whole life on a jury.

64
00:03:54,560 --> 00:03:56,940
I paid him like a private lawyer and he treated me like

65
00:03:56,940 --> 00:03:59,790
one more name on the list.

66
00:04:00,120 --> 00:04:01,520
Paid or free, it felt the same.

67
00:04:01,520 --> 00:04:04,370
The deal was already decided before he ever met.

68
00:04:07,300 --> 00:04:12,000
So I plead. Two years of probation, a restraining order,

69
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:15,140
close to $10 ,000 and all, between him, the restitution,

70
00:04:15,140 --> 00:04:18,400
and the fees. Before all of this, I was on our own.

71
00:04:18,400 --> 00:04:20,630
I didn't dream. I didn't do drugs.

72
00:04:21,660 --> 00:04:24,260
I was the girl teachers didn't work with.

73
00:04:24,260 --> 00:04:27,980
After, I was a 17 -year -old paying off a criminal case,

74
00:04:27,980 --> 00:04:30,920
lawyer payments, restitution, court costs, probation fees,

75
00:04:30,920 --> 00:04:34,550
anger management classes I paid for myself.

76
00:04:34,940 --> 00:04:37,200
The no contact order and the charges on my record kept

77
00:04:37,200 --> 00:04:38,420
me out of regular jobs.

78
00:04:38,420 --> 00:04:40,800
Nobody with an application in the back of my check -in

79
00:04:40,800 --> 00:04:44,140
ticket. So I took whatever worked for the payment, and

80
00:04:44,140 --> 00:04:46,780
I took all of it out of the ditch.

81
00:04:46,780 --> 00:04:48,090
I was just on site.

82
00:04:48,560 --> 00:04:52,530
When I went at all, I left with a 1 .5 and I barely graduated.

83
00:04:53,060 --> 00:04:54,750
That's what the deal cost.

84
00:04:55,040 --> 00:04:56,590
Not just the money.

85
00:04:57,200 --> 00:04:59,160
The girl I was going to be.

86
00:04:59,160 --> 00:05:01,530
The record cleared, I didn't.

87
00:05:02,500 --> 00:05:06,500
For years, I walked into every room expecting someone

88
00:05:06,500 --> 00:05:17,630
to point at me. Now, my cousin Tasha is the strong one.

89
00:05:18,200 --> 00:05:21,400
She works doubles, pays her own way.

90
00:05:21,400 --> 00:05:23,860
She lives on the street where two houses got shot at the

91
00:05:23,860 --> 00:05:27,000
summer before. She didn't have a license for a gun in

92
00:05:27,000 --> 00:05:30,480
her purse. She had it because she was tired of being afraid

93
00:05:30,480 --> 00:05:32,130
to walk to her car.

94
00:05:32,920 --> 00:05:45,050
At a party, her boyfriend got jumped.

95
00:05:46,980 --> 00:05:48,780
Three men had him on the ground.

96
00:05:48,780 --> 00:05:50,280
Kicking his head, she screamed.

97
00:05:50,280 --> 00:05:52,810
Nobody stopped. Six shots.

98
00:05:53,260 --> 00:05:57,140
One hit a man who was stomping him, and one hit the man

99
00:05:57,140 --> 00:05:58,570
she was trying to save.

100
00:05:58,980 --> 00:06:01,770
TASHA: I told them they were killing him, they said.

101
00:06:01,940 --> 00:06:03,350
OFFICER: Then why'd you keep shooting?

102
00:06:04,100 --> 00:06:07,150
Then all they wanted to talk about was the gun.

103
00:06:08,960 --> 00:06:11,650
Her lawyer had her case and about a hundred others.

104
00:06:11,900 --> 00:06:15,160
He told her that without a license, self -defense was

105
00:06:15,160 --> 00:06:20,970
a hard sell. He told her what 20 years sounds like.

106
00:06:21,120 --> 00:06:23,480
And here's what scared her the most.

107
00:06:23,480 --> 00:06:25,610
The gun was a gift.

108
00:06:25,860 --> 00:06:27,290
It was found with her.

109
00:06:27,640 --> 00:06:29,270
And that's all the record said.

110
00:06:29,400 --> 00:06:32,000
Nothing in the discovery showed what else could come with

111
00:06:32,000 --> 00:06:36,590
it. So the prosecutor was holding a blank check.

112
00:06:37,560 --> 00:06:40,570
Any day, one charge could turn into five.

113
00:06:40,960 --> 00:06:44,720
Fighting meant betting her whole life on what she couldn't

114
00:06:44,720 --> 00:06:48,170
see. I told her, say it was self -defense.

115
00:06:48,480 --> 00:06:50,980
Say it out loud. Make them answer it.

116
00:06:50,980 --> 00:06:52,890
But she was scared.

117
00:06:53,180 --> 00:06:54,430
And who wouldn't be?

118
00:06:54,640 --> 00:06:58,990
I took the plea. I just wanted to come home.

119
00:06:59,520 --> 00:07:03,180
She came home with a record and a question she'll carry

120
00:07:03,180 --> 00:07:06,170
forever. What if I had said it?

121
00:07:11,620 --> 00:07:13,250
Marcus is the baby.

122
00:07:15,040 --> 00:07:16,930
Sixteen, seventeen soon.

123
00:07:17,560 --> 00:07:19,910
He plays the video games with my son.

124
00:07:21,540 --> 00:07:24,750
Two boys from his school got shot that year.

125
00:07:25,760 --> 00:07:27,150
He stopped taking the bus.

126
00:07:27,180 --> 00:07:31,040
Too young to carry legally, but old enough to be scared

127
00:07:31,040 --> 00:07:36,100
to death. The police came with a warrant at six in the

128
00:07:36,100 --> 00:07:41,980
morning, found a gun in bed that wasn't registered to

129
00:07:41,980 --> 00:07:49,830
anyone. Just tell me it's yours and this all goes away.

130
00:07:51,320 --> 00:07:54,800
No parent in the room, no lawyer yet, a 16 -year -old

131
00:07:54,800 --> 00:07:58,250
who wanted it to be over, he said it was his.

132
00:07:59,500 --> 00:08:02,760
By the time his lawyer met him, that one sentence was

133
00:08:02,760 --> 00:08:07,280
the whole case. Nobody asked him why a 16 -year -old felt

134
00:08:07,280 --> 00:08:10,190
he needed a gun just to get to school.

135
00:08:10,560 --> 00:08:13,920
No contest. He was sent to placement two hours from his

136
00:08:13,920 --> 00:08:16,360
home. The record said one thing.

137
00:08:16,360 --> 00:08:18,070
A gun was found with him.

138
00:08:18,540 --> 00:08:22,260
Nothing more. Just a warning that if anything else came

139
00:08:22,260 --> 00:08:24,950
back, it would all get worse.

140
00:08:25,740 --> 00:08:29,200
A boy and his grandmother asked to bet against a blank

141
00:08:29,200 --> 00:08:32,830
page. They didn't even let him sit.

142
00:08:35,560 --> 00:08:38,350
I'm not saying none of us did anything.

143
00:08:38,480 --> 00:08:40,320
Guns without papers are still against the law.

144
00:08:40,320 --> 00:08:43,250
I didn't want one more child carrying one.

145
00:08:43,420 --> 00:08:46,970
I'm saying nobody asked what happened or why.

146
00:08:47,400 --> 00:08:49,270
Before, they offered us the deal.

147
00:08:49,740 --> 00:08:51,310
So here's what I teach my children.

148
00:08:51,720 --> 00:08:55,200
You can stay silent, say I want a lawyer, and that's that's

149
00:08:55,200 --> 00:08:58,790
all. If you're under 18, ask for your parent.

150
00:08:59,200 --> 00:09:01,860
If you're defending yourself or anyone else, tell your

151
00:09:01,860 --> 00:09:05,280
lawyer everything. Whether your lawyer is paid or free,

152
00:09:05,280 --> 00:09:09,330
they work for you. Ask them, have you heard my whole side?

153
00:09:09,380 --> 00:09:13,350
And if they haven't, make them sit down and listen.

154
00:09:13,920 --> 00:09:15,850
Write it out and hand it to them.

155
00:09:16,220 --> 00:09:18,390
Don't sign anything you don't understand.

156
00:09:19,020 --> 00:09:22,770
Ask what it will do to your life in 10 years.

157
00:09:22,880 --> 00:09:24,930
Before you take any deal, ask your lawyer.

158
00:09:25,520 --> 00:09:27,170
Have we seen all the evidence?

159
00:09:27,960 --> 00:09:30,050
Defend the poor and fatherless.

160
00:09:30,520 --> 00:09:32,770
Do justice to the afflicted and needy.

161
00:09:33,740 --> 00:09:38,240
Psalm 82, verse 3. The Lord executeth righteousness and

162
00:09:38,240 --> 00:09:40,810
judgment for all that are oppressed.

163
00:09:41,700 --> 00:09:43,940
Psalm 103, verse 6.

164
00:09:43,940 --> 00:09:46,870
The Lord also will be a refuge for the oppressed.

165
00:09:47,580 --> 00:09:49,870
A refuge in times of trouble.

166
00:09:50,240 --> 00:09:53,820
Psalm 9, verse 9. The Lord sees the room with the table

167
00:09:53,820 --> 00:09:54,680
and the two chairs.

168
00:09:54,680 --> 00:09:57,120
He sees the street where you live, and He sees who has

169
00:09:57,120 --> 00:10:00,740
never asked. Did your lawyer ever ask you what really

170
